Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||09-04-2000||09:58 PM||||my grandfather used to build ford race motors (flathead v8's and such) and from one of his discussions i learned that way back when you could take the heads, cover them with valve grinding compound and rub it on glass until it turned dull grey, then do the same to the engine block, torque it back on, and voila' more compression, no weak head gasket. out of curiousity, would this work on our cars, maybe for people with turbos so as not to but head gaskets, or just to up compression? (he showed me on his t-bucket roadster how to do it, so i know its real)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||5
